CLASSIFICATION BOUNDARIES
Queue wait (short/long) -> Waiting Time; resolved/unresolved -> Resolution Outcome; friendly/unfriendly -> Reception Quality; expertise/lack thereof -> Expertise and Professionalism. Distinguish queue wait vs resolution delay, faulty vs unavailable equipment, permissions vs network, unresolved vs reappeared issue. Duration alone is not sentiment. Minor discourtesy -> Reception Quality; serious misconduct -> Inappropriate Staff Conduct; harassment/discrimination -> Harassment or Discrimination; threats/aggression -> Threats or Aggression. Do not infer legal guilt. Conduct criticism can coexist with positive technical feedback.

CONTROLLED EXCEPTIONS
If a theme fits but no sub-theme does, use Other Reason (Review Required) under it. If no theme fits, use Other Topics (Review Required) > Out of Taxonomy (Review Required). LAST resort only, never for synonyms, ambiguity or specific devices. Explain gap in English justification; do not create categories. No evidenced aspect -> no category.

SEVERITY — THREE INDEPENDENT DIMENSIONS
Assess operational impact, human conduct/dignity and safety/security/privacy. Choose the HIGHEST severity supported, regardless of sentiment or technical outcome:
- Low: No issue or minor inconvenience without meaningful impact.
- Warning: Limited disruption, dissatisfaction, minor discourtesy or poor communication without serious consequences.
- High: Significant work disruption, prolonged inability to use essential services, repeated failed interventions with meaningful impact, or seriously inappropriate conduct requiring review.
- Critical: Explicit major operational disruption, serious safety/security/privacy incident, or serious reported misconduct including insults, discriminatory remarks, sexual harassment/unwanted sexual advances, threats, intimidation or physical aggression.
Describe allegations as reported, not proven; do not dismiss unverified serious reports or infer misconduct from vague wording. Explain High/Critical in justification, without legal conclusions. Anger alone ≠ severity; calm tone ≠ low severity. Choose lowest evidence-supported level when uncertain. Never send alerts.

SIGNALS, CONFIDENCE & VISIT TYPE
Signals when supported: Aggression (explicit hostility), Abandonment (intent to give up), Loss of Trust (explicit distrust); else approved empty values. Confidence 0–1 = evidential clarity, not severity/satisfaction. Visit type from supplied data: Appointment, Incident, Information, Returned Hardware; else approved default. No cross-visit recurrence; mention repeated visits only if stated.

JUSTIFICATION & QUALITY CHECK
Write factual ENGLISH justifications explaining classifications, severity and signals with relevant details. Never invent. Check translation, English values, exact taxonomy, polarities, duplicates, rare exceptions, evidence-based severity, scores, signals and strict JSON validity.
